{"content":[{"c":["BETH-AVEN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Town in Benjamin’s territory, located west of Michmash on the border of the wilderness, near Ai, to the east of Bethel (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.7.2","r":"Josh.7.2","rawR":"Josh.7.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.7.2","value":"Josh.7.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 7:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.18.12","r":"Josh.18.12","rawR":"Josh.18.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.18.12","value":"Josh.18.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.13.5","r":"1Sam.13.5","rawR":"1Sam.13.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.13.5","value":"1Sam.13.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 13:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.14.23","r":"1Sam.14.23","rawR":"1Sam.14.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.14.23","value":"1Sam.14.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:23"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Term used by Hosea contemptuously to refer to Bethel, an ancient center of worship, because the “House of God” (Bethel) had become a “house of wickedness” (Beth-aven or just Aven; ",{"href":"?bref=Hos.4.15","r":"Hos.4.15","rawR":"Hos.4.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.4.15","value":"Hos.4.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hos 4:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Hos.5.8","r":"Hos.5.8","rawR":"Hos.5.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.5.8","value":"Hos.5.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Hos.10.5","r":"Hos.10.5","rawR":"Hos.10.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.10.5","value":"Hos.10.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:5"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Aven_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Aven_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Aven_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Aven #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BethAven","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 7:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.7.2","rawQueryValu